<%# What the server tells the nudge, and nothing else. #410.

    The same shape as _rest_cue and for the same reason: the nudge cannot live inside
    #session-body, because that region is replaced on every Done tap and every fifteen-second
    poll, and "how long have you been standing there" is state. So the bar sits outside and
    this carries the one fact it cannot work out for itself.

    Two facts, in fact, and they are different in kind. `last-at` is when the session last did
    anything, which is what the quiet is measured from. `quiet-after` is how long that quiet
    has to run before the question is worth asking, which comes off the rest prescribed for
    the set that was ticked off -- three times it, floored and capped. A block writing eight
    minutes between singles gets asked half an hour later rather than being interrupted while
    the lifter is still resting.

    **Unlike the rest cue, this one carries the session rather than the tap.** The rest cue is
    deliberately empty when a tap did not finish a set, because a mis-tap corrected is not the
    start of a rest. This is the opposite: it always says when the session last moved, whatever
    the tap did, because an un-complete is still the session doing something and the quiet has
    to restart from it. It is also filled in on first paint, so arriving at a session left open
    this morning is asked about immediately rather than in another twenty minutes.

    Empty where there is no quiet worth measuring, which is two sessions rather than one. A
    session with no completed set has no quiet to measure and nothing to close. A session the
    lifter has finished has plenty of quiet and nothing left to ask about: open this evening
    the session you trained this morning and the bar used to appear on first paint saying
    "nothing logged for 11h, still training?" -- which is #523, and the sentence its title is
    quoting. Both arrive here as a cue with no stamp on it, and the script draws nothing for
    either.

    `oob` is a local with a default so the two callers read the same way _rest_cue's do: the
    session view renders this plainly on first paint, the complete route renders it with
    oob: true. %>
<span id="quiet-cue"<%== ' hx-swap-oob="true"' if defined?(oob) && oob %> hidden
      data-last-at="<%= last_at %>" data-quiet-after="<%= quiet_after %>"></span>
